From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: hctosys: Clamp system clock to minimum epoch

The Qualcomm PMIC RTC on the Fossil Gen 6 (PM660) can return garbage
values (~860K seconds, i.e. January 1970) when the RTC registers have
never been properly initialized. Booting with the system clock at 1970
causes systemd to stall and the hardware watchdog to reset the device,
resulting in a boot crash loop.

Add a compile-time minimum epoch (CONFIG_RTC_HCTOSYS_MIN_YEAR, default
0 = disabled) so that if the RTC reads a value before that year, the
system clock is set to the minimum instead. This gives userspace
(systemd, timesyncd) a reasonable starting point. Once NTP syncs,
hwclock -w will write the correct time back to the RTC for future boots.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific workaround]
Signed-off-by: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
---
 drivers/rtc/Kconfig   |  9 +++++++++
 drivers/rtc/hctosys.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/Kconfig b/drivers/rtc/Kconfig
index acae8d23731f..bc0b007d3fd3 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/rtc/Kconfig
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@ config RTC_HCTOSYS_DEVICE
 	  sleep states. Do not specify an RTC here unless it stays powered
 	  during all this system's supported sleep states.

+config RTC_HCTOSYS_MIN_YEAR
+	int "Minimum year for RTC hctosys (0 = no minimum)"
+	default 0
+	help
+	  If the RTC reads a date before January 1 of this year, hctosys
+	  will clamp the system clock to that date instead. This prevents
+	  boot failures caused by uninitialized or corrupted RTC values.
+	  Set to 0 to disable the check (default).
+
 config RTC_SYSTOHC
 	bool "Set the RTC time based on NTP synchronization"
 	default y
diff --git a/drivers/rtc/hctosys.c b/drivers/rtc/hctosys.c
index b9ec4a16db1f..1472f8f1dd46 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/hctosys.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/hctosys.c
@@ -49,6 +49,18 @@ static int __init rtc_hctosys(void)

 	tv64.tv_sec = rtc_tm_to_time64(&tm);

+#if defined(CONFIG_RTC_HCTOSYS_MIN_YEAR) && CONFIG_RTC_HCTOSYS_MIN_YEAR > 0
+	{
+		time64_t min_epoch = mktime64(CONFIG_RTC_HCTOSYS_MIN_YEAR, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0);
+		if (tv64.tv_sec < min_epoch) {
+			dev_warn(rtc->dev.parent,
+				"hctosys: RTC value %lld is before %d, clamping to %lld\n",
+				(long long)tv64.tv_sec, CONFIG_RTC_HCTOSYS_MIN_YEAR, (long long)min_epoch);
+			tv64.tv_sec = min_epoch;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 #if BITS_PER_LONG == 32
 	if (tv64.tv_sec > INT_MAX) {
 		err = -ERANGE;
